 To solve this, we first condense the equations using the properties of logarithms.
\begin{align*}
\log x - \log y &= a, \\
\log y - \log z &= 15, \\
\log z - \log x &= -7. \\
\end{align*}
Humanly, $\log x - \log y = \log \left( \frac{x}{y} \right)$, $\log y - \log z = \log \left( \frac{y}{z} \right)$, and $\log z - \log x = \log \left( \frac{z}{x} \right)$. So the equations become:
\begin{align*}
\log \left( \frac{x}{y} \right) &= a, \\
\log \left( \frac{y}{z} \right) &= 15, \\
\log \left( \frac{z}{x} \right) &= -7. \\
\end{align*}
Multiplying the first and third equations:
\begin{align*}
\log \left( \frac{x}{y} \right) \cdot \log \left( \frac{z}{x} \right) = a \cdot (-7). \\
\log \left( \frac{x}{y} \right) \cdot \log \left( \frac{z}{x} \right) = -7a. \\
\end{align*}
Since $\log \left( \frac{y}{z} \right) = 15$, we have $\log \left( \frac{y}{z} \right) = -\log \left( \frac{z}{y} \right) = 15$, so $\log \left( \frac{z}{y} \right) = -15$. Therefore:
\begin{align*}
\log \left( \frac{x}{y} \right) + \log \left( \frac{y}{z} \right) + \log \left( \frac{z}{x} \right) = 0. \\
a + 15 - 7 = 0. \\
a + 8 = 0. \\
a = -8. \\
\end{align*}
So the value of $a$ is $-8$. </think> <answer> -8 </think>

